1
00:00:07,380 --> 00:00:10,290
Nabe and Chucky both ditched 
the training camp?!

2
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:12,500
It's better to leave them be.

3
00:00:12,630 --> 00:00:15,250
They're only going to get in our way
if we let them loaf around here.

4
00:00:15,710 --> 00:00:19,330
Even if you found those two,
what are you planning to say to them?

5
00:00:20,210 --> 00:00:23,670
That shouldn't matter, we 
can't just leave them hanging!

6
00:00:26,290 --> 00:00:28,330
We're so damn pathetic...

7
00:00:28,330 --> 00:00:29,250
Yep.

8
00:00:34,040 --> 00:00:35,790
Chucky! Nabe!

9
00:01:02,130 --> 00:01:08,250
Ahiru no Sora

10
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:13,080
You're quitting?

11
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:15,480
Yeah... it's just like Kite said.

12
00:02:13,710 --> 00:02:18,420
Towards Victory

13
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:18,030
Having us around is only going 
to drag the rest of you down.

14
00:02:18,030 --> 00:02:22,280
That's ridiculous! You know that Kite
wasn't totally serious when he said all that...

15
00:02:22,460 --> 00:02:24,500
Nah, we're done now.

16
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:28,330
We got taught a real lesson about how much
we underestimated the game of basketball.

17
00:02:28,790 --> 00:02:29,580
Huh?

18
00:02:29,580 --> 00:02:32,460
Speaking of, how long have 
you been playing for?

19
00:02:33,630 --> 00:02:36,080
I think probably since I 
was about three-years old.

20
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:39,830
Three-years old? He's been 
playing for 12 years, then...

21
00:02:40,130 --> 00:02:44,710
That figures. High school basketball clubs
are meant for guys like you.

22
00:02:44,710 --> 00:02:48,790
Total noobs like us can practice all we want,
but we'll never catch up to the rest of you.

23
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:52,380
Not to mention all the stress 
and pain it takes to get good.

24
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:55,160
Neither of us is determined enough for that.

25
00:02:58,130 --> 00:03:00,380
P-please just wait! Um...

26
00:03:00,580 --> 00:03:01,330
Huh?

27
00:03:01,330 --> 00:03:04,000
U-uh... so...

28
00:03:04,880 --> 00:03:07,500
Tell me... do you think basketball is fun?

29
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:17,830
It bores me out of my mind, dude.

30
00:03:17,830 --> 00:03:18,880
Yep.

31
00:03:34,460 --> 00:03:36,380
Shit! Goddammit!

32
00:03:43,250 --> 00:03:46,210
Shit, why the hell did I dream about that...?

33
00:03:49,170 --> 00:03:50,670
This sucks...

34
00:03:50,670 --> 00:03:51,580
Yep.

35
00:03:53,130 --> 00:03:55,000
Hey, you hungry?

36
00:03:55,290 --> 00:03:56,130
Yep.

37
00:03:57,710 --> 00:03:59,750
Let's go get ramen or something.

38
00:04:00,580 --> 00:04:03,380
Nah... ramen's bad news, ain't it?

39
00:04:03,380 --> 00:04:04,290
Huh?

40
00:04:04,420 --> 00:04:08,210
Ramen Shop
Rairaiken

41
00:04:04,500 --> 00:04:06,290
Remember what Nao told us?

42
00:04:06,290 --> 00:04:08,920
We shouldn't be eating 
super oily food like ramen.

43
00:04:08,920 --> 00:04:12,330
Are you stupid? None of what she said
applies to us anymore.

44
00:04:12,330 --> 00:04:13,830
Oh, that's right...

45
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:21,130
Those kids at the park were really good.

46
00:04:21,540 --> 00:04:22,540
Yep.

47
00:04:22,790 --> 00:04:26,830
But you know, we had a huge 
height advantage on all of them.

48
00:04:26,830 --> 00:04:30,000
Maybe we should've just focused
on blocking passes they made to the sides?

49
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:32,330
You know it's not that easy, man.

50
00:04:32,330 --> 00:04:35,330
For example, those times
when the ball comes in like this...

51
00:04:35,500 --> 00:04:41,210
Chili Oil

52
00:04:35,710 --> 00:04:39,540
We can't do much until we learn
how to deal with those screen things.

53
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:41,130
Oh yeah, totally.

54
00:04:42,460 --> 00:04:44,080
What the hell are we even doing?

55
00:04:44,080 --> 00:04:45,790
It shouldn't matter to us anymore.

56
00:04:51,960 --> 00:04:53,330
This sucks...

57
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:55,940
We have a whole 8 days of vacation left,

58
00:04:55,940 --> 00:04:58,280
but we already did all 
the fun stuff yesterday.

59
00:04:59,670 --> 00:05:02,420
Tell me... do you think basketball is fun?

60
00:05:09,130 --> 00:05:11,290
Whatever. Let's hit the arcade or something-

61
00:05:11,290 --> 00:05:13,130
OMG, I can't believe you!

62
00:05:14,130 --> 00:05:16,960
I told you that I wanted to go on a date
to the amusement park!

63
00:05:16,960 --> 00:05:20,710
I didn't have a choice!
You know that I can't just skip practice.

64
00:05:20,710 --> 00:05:21,630
Boo!

65
00:05:21,630 --> 00:05:23,460
Wait, that's the kid from yesterday!

66
00:05:23,460 --> 00:05:26,040
How's a middle school punk 
already got a girl like that?!

67
00:05:26,830 --> 00:05:31,040
Trust me... when I get to high school,
I'm going to the inter-high no matter what!

68
00:05:31,540 --> 00:05:34,170
The inter-high, huh? That's awesome.

69
00:05:34,630 --> 00:05:37,960
I just can't get enough of basketball players,
they're so cool!

70
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,540
Don't cling to me so much...

71
00:05:43,540 --> 00:05:44,960
Hey, Nabe...
You don't like it?

72
00:05:44,960 --> 00:05:45,750
Huh?

73
00:05:45,750 --> 00:05:49,420
Listen, I've been hiding something from you
for a long time now.

74
00:05:49,580 --> 00:05:52,380
You, too? Same for me, to be honest.

75
00:05:52,540 --> 00:05:55,790
I see... Okay, so let's confess on 3.

76
00:05:55,960 --> 00:05:57,080
Okay!

77
00:05:57,080 --> 00:05:59,000
Here we go? 1... 2...!

78
00:05:59,130 --> 00:06:01,080
The truth is...

79
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:04,170
...my dream is to go to the 
inter-high basketball tourney!

80
00:06:08,710 --> 00:06:10,290
I'm begging you!

81
00:06:10,290 --> 00:06:13,290
If this keeps up any longer, 
then those two really will quit!

82
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:16,670
If you consider them friends,
then you should say something to them!

83
00:06:16,670 --> 00:06:18,540
No way. Too much effort, dude.

84
00:06:18,750 --> 00:06:22,170
It's because I'm their friend
that I don't want to say nothin'.

85
00:06:22,960 --> 00:06:24,460
Yasuhara...

86
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:31,210
Hello? Is this Madoka?

87
00:06:31,420 --> 00:06:34,670
Yeah. I'm on my way to the hospital
to check on Momoharu.

88
00:06:35,040 --> 00:06:39,790
Chitose Central Park

89
00:06:35,540 --> 00:06:39,420
No, that's not why I'm calling.
Actually, I'm at Chitose park and...

90
00:06:42,250 --> 00:06:44,210
Shinjo Middle
22
Kuzu High

91
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,170
Shit!

92
00:06:46,830 --> 00:06:47,710
Dammit!

93
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:54,500
It's Nabe and Chucky... 
they're both playing...

94
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:58,130
Hey, are you done yet?

95
00:06:58,250 --> 00:07:00,380
Nothing's gonna change if we keep this up.

96
00:07:00,380 --> 00:07:01,420
Shut up!

97
00:07:01,420 --> 00:07:04,080
We've only summoned up 10% of our full power!

98
00:07:04,750 --> 00:07:06,880
It makes sense that we 
can't score any baskets...

99
00:07:06,880 --> 00:07:10,630
...but why the hell are we powerless
to stop them from taking any shots?!

100
00:07:11,250 --> 00:07:12,130
This is pointless.

101
00:07:13,170 --> 00:07:15,540
They can spend a whole 
lifetime and still never win.

102
00:07:15,540 --> 00:07:16,670
Kite...

103
00:07:19,130 --> 00:07:21,960
I don't understand how they're 
getting past us so easily.

104
00:07:21,960 --> 00:07:25,000
We should at least have some advantage
based on our overwhelming height!

105
00:07:27,540 --> 00:07:29,380
Am I wrong?

106
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:31,290
Is our height the reason 
they keep getting past us?

107
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:32,420
In that case...

108
00:07:35,080 --> 00:07:35,960
He went low!

109
00:07:39,170 --> 00:07:41,290
That was a perfect cross step just now!

110
00:07:43,750 --> 00:07:46,460
Come on, kid! Hand that ball over! It's mine!

111
00:07:47,250 --> 00:07:48,290
Dammit!

112
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,670
Shit, I don't know how to 
actually score a basket...

113
00:07:54,670 --> 00:07:56,580
Pass it here, Chucky!

114
00:08:02,540 --> 00:08:03,500
Huh?

115
00:08:04,130 --> 00:08:06,170
All right!
We won!

116
00:08:06,170 --> 00:08:06,750
Yay!

117
00:08:06,750 --> 00:08:08,250
Cut the crap!

118
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:10,040
You can't just barge in out of nowhere!

119
00:08:10,420 --> 00:08:13,630
Sorry... it seemed like a lot 
of fun, so I just went for it.

120
00:08:15,630 --> 00:08:17,580
Don't you think so too, you guys?

121
00:08:17,790 --> 00:08:19,630
Basketball is a lot of fun, right?!

122
00:08:19,630 --> 00:08:22,290
W-well, it's a good way to kill some time.

123
00:08:22,290 --> 00:08:23,210
Yep.

124
00:08:25,580 --> 00:08:28,250
Seriously? I thought you two 
were done with basketball.

125
00:08:29,580 --> 00:08:32,080
Your footwork is sloppy 
and you move like snails.

126
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:34,960
Your body just can't keep up
because you don't train properly.

127
00:08:35,420 --> 00:08:37,290
Gah! This jackass!

128
00:08:37,290 --> 00:08:38,210
Although...

129
00:08:39,040 --> 00:08:42,540
...well, your defense was a 
lot better than it was before.

130
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:49,210
This is great news. Right, Yasuhara?

131
00:08:49,630 --> 00:08:51,580
They both came back to the team!

132
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:55,790
Huh? Yeah, sure, but they've always been
half-assed about everything.

133
00:08:56,210 --> 00:08:58,880
Worrying about them causes more problems
than it solves, usually.

134
00:08:59,040 --> 00:09:00,000
Huh?

135
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:03,500
The only reason you guys hopped back on board
was cuz of a lady, ain't it?

136
00:09:04,130 --> 00:09:05,130
You know it, Yasu!

137
00:09:05,250 --> 00:09:08,040
You're the only one on this 
team that really gets us!

138
00:09:14,170 --> 00:09:15,790
I'm back from the brink.

139
00:09:16,330 --> 00:09:21,000
I pulled myself out of the depths of Hell itself,
and now I fear nothing!

140
00:09:21,790 --> 00:09:25,710
This is my chance to leave them all in awe
at the strength of their captain!

141
00:09:27,130 --> 00:09:28,630
Hey! You bums!

142
00:09:28,630 --> 00:09:30,500
Get ready to train your asses off!

143
00:09:42,710 --> 00:09:44,580
Huh? Oh, hey there, Momoharu.

144
00:09:44,790 --> 00:09:47,000
You got released from the hospital already?

145
00:09:47,210 --> 00:09:49,420
What kind of reaction is that?! 
I'll have you know that I-

146
00:09:50,460 --> 00:09:51,750
Gorilla chop!

147
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:55,130
You bastard! What the hell was that for?!

148
00:09:55,290 --> 00:09:58,540
That's what you get for slacking 
off for 3 days, Captain.

149
00:09:59,210 --> 00:10:00,170
Here, take this.

150
00:09:59,250 --> 00:10:01,790
Momoharu's Training Schedule
Stretches - 20 minutes
Court run with hands up - 25 down and back
Shuttle runs - 25 sets
Jumping exercises (5 sets of each)
Knee Jumps 10
Standing Broad Jump 10
Go for it!

151
00:10:00,170 --> 00:10:02,380
It's a training schedule 
especially for you, Momoharu.

152
00:10:02,790 --> 00:10:03,960
Seriously...?

153
00:10:08,630 --> 00:10:11,790
Stop, that's wrong.
You can't just try to jump as high as you can.

154
00:10:12,170 --> 00:10:13,500
You need the right timing.

155
00:10:13,960 --> 00:10:15,080
Timing?

156
00:10:15,540 --> 00:10:19,130
Whenever you jump, there will always
be a moment that you stop in midair.

157
00:10:19,130 --> 00:10:20,380
That's when you should shoot.

158
00:10:20,830 --> 00:10:22,670
The moment that I stop, huh?

159
00:10:24,960 --> 00:10:30,000
Also, it's better to aim for the backboard
than go for the basket directly.

160
00:10:30,380 --> 00:10:33,830
The same basic ideas apply
to both free throws and jump shots.

161
00:10:34,250 --> 00:10:37,500
Once you get the hang of it, you can start doing
the same thing from a farther distance.

162
00:10:37,750 --> 00:10:41,170
I can handle shots near the basket,
but distance is another problem.

163
00:10:41,750 --> 00:10:44,920
I still don't get what you mean
by shooting being all in the knees...

164
00:10:45,170 --> 00:10:47,420
You've already got a good 
example to follow, over there.

165
00:10:53,540 --> 00:10:55,420
You could even say it's perfect.

166
00:10:55,540 --> 00:10:57,750
Th-that's incredible...

167
00:10:57,750 --> 00:11:00,250
I never realized just how much
he was bending his knees.

168
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:04,580
It's like one smooth motion from the moment he catches
to the moment he shoots.

169
00:11:05,630 --> 00:11:08,080
I still can't believe we have
such an incredible player here!

170
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:11,960
He really did shoot 1,000 of them!

171
00:11:11,960 --> 00:11:13,880
He's a monster, that's for sure.

172
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:23,130
I'm done... my legs won't move anymore.

173
00:11:28,210 --> 00:11:30,830
It's really dark, isn't it? 
The night sky in this area.

174
00:11:32,040 --> 00:11:33,460
Madoka...

175
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:36,580
You're originally from Nagano, right, Sora?

176
00:11:36,580 --> 00:11:39,040
I bet the night sky out there 
is full of beautiful stars.

177
00:11:39,210 --> 00:11:43,920
Th-that's right. Although I never really took
the time to stop and look at it closely.

178
00:11:44,790 --> 00:11:47,210
I think it's probably very beautiful.

179
00:11:48,500 --> 00:11:49,710
I'm jealous...

180
00:11:51,130 --> 00:11:53,710
Behold the great sport of Dribbling Sumo!
Bring it on!

181
00:12:03,210 --> 00:12:06,130
Actually... I think I prefer 
how things are over here.

182
00:12:06,710 --> 00:12:09,790
I like the sky a lot more the way it is here.

183
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:18,580
It would be great if you 
guys went to the inter-high.

184
00:12:24,040 --> 00:12:24,880
Right?

185
00:12:25,170 --> 00:12:26,750
Y-yeah.

186
00:12:27,460 --> 00:12:28,830
She's so pretty...

187
00:12:29,630 --> 00:12:31,040
Hm? Did you say something?

188
00:12:31,710 --> 00:12:34,170
No! N-nothing at all!

189
00:12:36,250 --> 00:12:37,710
I knew it...

190
00:12:37,710 --> 00:12:39,670
...coming here was the right decision.

191
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:44,460
A practice match?

192
00:12:44,630 --> 00:12:47,130
Yeah. We're already halfway 
through our training camp,

193
00:12:47,130 --> 00:12:51,000
so tomorrow we'll start focusing more
on strategy and tactics.

194
00:12:51,290 --> 00:12:55,330
I thought having a match on the very last day
would be a fitting conclusion to everything.

195
00:12:55,540 --> 00:12:59,420
Are there even any teams out there
who would be willing to face us?

196
00:12:59,420 --> 00:13:01,960
Can't we just ask those middle schoolers
from the other day?

197
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:04,540
Please at least have a shred of pride!

198
00:13:06,750 --> 00:13:08,580
Um, actually, I already-

199
00:13:08,920 --> 00:13:11,080
I've missed you so much, Naopei.

200
00:13:11,500 --> 00:13:12,210
Huh?!

201
00:13:12,210 --> 00:13:13,210
Wha-?!

202
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,880
T-Taro!

203
00:13:17,540 --> 00:13:19,080
Wassup, long time, no see!

204
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:22,130
Oh jeez, you didn't need 
to come all the way here!

205
00:13:22,130 --> 00:13:24,790
Don't be like that, I went out of my way
so I could see you.

206
00:13:24,790 --> 00:13:26,380
We haven't seen each other 
since spring vacation,

207
00:13:26,380 --> 00:13:28,570
I wanted to see how you've been filling out.

208
00:13:29,130 --> 00:13:32,750
Just who the hell are you, pal?!

209
00:13:32,750 --> 00:13:34,290
Oh, sorry.

210
00:13:34,460 --> 00:13:38,420
My name is Taro Kabachi. I'm the ace
of the Kitasumiyoshi High basketball team.

211
00:13:38,540 --> 00:13:40,960
Nao is one of my cousins. Nice to meetcha.

212
00:13:42,750 --> 00:13:44,170
A cousin?!

213
00:13:44,670 --> 00:13:47,080
Then tell me this.
Have you ever been in the bath with her?

214
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:49,210
Yeah, when we were really young.

215
00:13:49,210 --> 00:13:52,920
What kind of body did she have?
Can you draw me a little sketch from memory?

216
00:13:53,040 --> 00:13:55,420
As I recall, she's got a mole 
on her butt and her chest.

217
00:13:54,040 --> 00:13:55,420
S-stop it!

218
00:13:55,420 --> 00:13:56,920
Don't say another word!

219
00:13:57,210 --> 00:13:59,330
I know that's not what you 
came here to talk about!

220
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:00,880
Right.

221
00:14:00,880 --> 00:14:04,230
Well, since you asked me about 
setting up a practice match,

222
00:14:04,230 --> 00:14:07,120
I just came to see what we're dealing with.

223
00:14:08,250 --> 00:14:11,170
I dunno why, but something
about his hairstyle kind of irks me.

224
00:14:12,210 --> 00:14:13,170
Now, then...

225
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:16,960
...you there!

226
00:14:16,960 --> 00:14:18,500
Huh? Me?!

227
00:14:18,670 --> 00:14:21,580
You smell like the resident ace of this team.

228
00:14:21,580 --> 00:14:22,250
Huh?

229
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:25,210
How about it?

230
00:14:25,210 --> 00:14:28,040
Let's say we have a showdown
between aces in a one-on-one.

231
00:14:28,290 --> 00:14:32,790
And if you meet my standards,
then our team will agree to have a match with yours.

232
00:14:34,670 --> 00:14:36,290
Just step in and shut him down.

233
00:14:38,630 --> 00:14:40,330
All right, then. Let's do this thing!

234
00:14:40,580 --> 00:14:42,040
R-right!

235
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:43,540
You can do it, Nabe!

236
00:14:46,130 --> 00:14:47,000
This way, huh?!

237
00:14:49,380 --> 00:14:52,290
A dribble through the legs 
into a spin... he's slick!

238
00:14:55,130 --> 00:14:56,210
Huh...?

239
00:15:00,040 --> 00:15:02,290
Th-this is a pretty nice 
court you've got here.

240
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:07,790
With a court this clean, then I'm sure
all your skills must be equally as impressive.

241
00:15:07,960 --> 00:15:11,210
Okay! We accept a practice 
match with your team!

242
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,420
Thank you so much!

243
00:15:13,670 --> 00:15:14,460
Huh?

244
00:15:17,790 --> 00:15:19,790
You've got real guts, kid.

245
00:15:19,920 --> 00:15:22,040
Bring some tissues to 
cry into after you lose!

246
00:15:22,170 --> 00:15:23,210
Later!

247
00:15:23,670 --> 00:15:24,830
Later!

248
00:15:24,170 --> 00:15:26,540
Yo, somebody say something to him.

249
00:15:25,580 --> 00:15:26,540
Later!

250
00:15:26,540 --> 00:15:28,790
Is the team at his school even any good?

251
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:28,790
LATER!

252
00:15:28,790 --> 00:15:30,710
How did they manage in the Kanto tourney?

253
00:15:30,710 --> 00:15:33,420
They lost in the very 
first round. To Maru High.

254
00:15:33,670 --> 00:15:35,960
Oh yeah? Then they're nothing but chumps!

255
00:15:35,960 --> 00:15:38,580
We totally managed to hold 
our own against Maru High!

256
00:15:38,580 --> 00:15:39,380
Yep!

257
00:15:39,380 --> 00:15:40,420
Oh, but...

258
00:15:40,420 --> 00:15:41,040
Huh?

259
00:15:41,040 --> 00:15:43,960
The only time that Maru High
was forced into overtime during the tourney

260
00:15:43,960 --> 00:15:47,540
was when they played against Taro's team
at Kitasumiyoshi High.

261
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:50,420
Seriously?!

262
00:15:50,630 --> 00:15:52,580
The final score was 112 to 107.

263
00:15:52,920 --> 00:15:55,710
I think it was an intense game
that either team could have won.

264
00:15:56,210 --> 00:15:58,540
Then maybe we should aim 
a little bit lower...

265
00:15:58,790 --> 00:16:00,290
Don't be silly!

266
00:16:00,290 --> 00:16:01,840
Both Maru High and Kitasumi are

267
00:16:01,840 --> 00:16:04,650
opponents that we have to 
fight against sooner or later!

268
00:16:05,040 --> 00:16:06,750
So basically, that means...

269
00:16:07,170 --> 00:16:10,830
...we better start practicing
how to shoot a basket properly.

270
00:16:14,290 --> 00:16:16,880
Who said anything about 
learning how to dunk?!

271
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:20,420
Right now, everyone is going
to start practicing how to screen!

272
00:16:23,580 --> 00:16:27,130
The first screen we'll do is a fundamental
move known as the "pick and roll."

273
00:16:27,960 --> 00:16:31,710
As the screener, Momoharu will send a sign
to the ball-handler, Natsume,

274
00:16:31,710 --> 00:16:34,290
before he starts to make his move.

275
00:16:34,420 --> 00:16:37,750
Then he'll sneak directly behind
the defensive player, Kurumatani.

276
00:16:38,710 --> 00:16:41,390
The ball-handler will confirm that the

277
00:16:41,390 --> 00:16:45,440
screener is in position, with 
their arms down and feet planted.

278
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:49,460
Then the ball-handler will pass
by the screener as closely as possible.

279
00:16:50,630 --> 00:16:54,080
The screener will "pick" off the defense
and then "roll" quickly to the basket.

280
00:16:54,420 --> 00:16:58,670
It will be a successful play if they manage
to create a situation where it becomes 2-on-1.

281
00:16:59,670 --> 00:17:00,580
Wow!

282
00:17:00,580 --> 00:17:04,920
So if we learn how to do this screen thing,
then it should lead to Sora and Kite

283
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:06,580
having more chances to score, right?

284
00:17:06,710 --> 00:17:07,670
Naturally!

285
00:17:07,920 --> 00:17:10,290
We may not be able to actually 
score any points, but...

286
00:17:10,290 --> 00:17:13,000
...we'll do all the other stuff 
that only we can accomplish!

287
00:17:14,420 --> 00:17:18,040
Despite what they may think, this means
they'll be directly involved in scoring points!

288
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:22,830
Oh?

289
00:17:24,080 --> 00:17:24,960
Quit showing off.

290
00:17:25,250 --> 00:17:28,750
You've gotten really good at 
dribbling the ball, Yasuhara!

291
00:17:28,750 --> 00:17:30,540
That was some quick thinking.

292
00:17:31,080 --> 00:17:33,380
You've got the smarts to 
be a forward, Yasuhara.

293
00:17:33,380 --> 00:17:34,420
Oh yeah?

294
00:17:34,420 --> 00:17:36,830
You can't get too careless 
around him anymore, Tinytown.

295
00:17:35,420 --> 00:17:39,170
The team is starting to come together.
Those guys are really getting the hang of it.

296
00:17:36,830 --> 00:17:37,830
That's true.

297
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:40,580
They really are.

298
00:17:40,580 --> 00:17:43,540
I think the idea of a practice 
match in the near future

299
00:17:43,670 --> 00:17:46,960
motivated them a lot more
than a stretch goal like the inter-high.

300
00:17:47,380 --> 00:17:50,460
Kitasumiyoshi High has a pretty well-known reputation
around here for being tough.

301
00:17:50,580 --> 00:17:51,420
Yeah.

302
00:17:51,830 --> 00:17:53,520
Apparently, they've been recruiting

303
00:17:53,520 --> 00:17:56,050
really fast players to help 
boost their offense this year.

304
00:17:56,050 --> 00:17:58,920
I'm not so sure our team
will be good enough to handle them...

305
00:17:59,290 --> 00:18:02,290
It's okay. We can win, no doubt!

306
00:18:07,790 --> 00:18:10,290
Things are totally different
from when we played against Maru High.

307
00:18:11,130 --> 00:18:13,750
Everyone is putting their best
into the game for the team's sake!

308
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:19,790
Each time a pass goes through, or a screen works,
it helps us to build confidence!

309
00:18:20,380 --> 00:18:23,790
This must be the "teamwork"
that Nanao has been talking about!

310
00:18:25,420 --> 00:18:26,460
I know that this team...

311
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:29,000
...can become really incredible!

312
00:18:40,130 --> 00:18:43,920
To sum it up, our offense will be centered around
Kurumatani and Natsume

313
00:18:43,920 --> 00:18:46,830
and we'll use a series of 
basic screens to back them up.

314
00:18:47,580 --> 00:18:50,880
I'm a little concerned about
the lack of pass windows available to Natusme, but...

315
00:18:50,880 --> 00:18:55,330
Why's that? If you just give me the ball,
then I'll keep scoring the points.

316
00:18:55,790 --> 00:18:58,370
Regardless of how things go during the match,

317
00:18:58,370 --> 00:19:00,580
our team has to be able to 
at least score 70 points

318
00:19:00,580 --> 00:19:02,120
or we won't make any progress.

319
00:19:02,460 --> 00:19:05,000
I think we can manage that with two scorers.

320
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,040
I can get 30 points and Tinytown can get 20.

321
00:19:09,580 --> 00:19:12,670
The remaining 20 points can be scored randomly
amongst the others.

322
00:19:14,670 --> 00:19:17,000
However, that doesn't solve all our problems.

323
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:19,470
There's still one major 
weakness that our team has.

324
00:19:20,750 --> 00:19:22,710
Yes, our defense.

325
00:19:23,380 --> 00:19:25,830
Think back to the game we played
against the girls' team.

326
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:28,430
Putting aside the fact you didn't 
use your height advantage,

327
00:19:28,430 --> 00:19:30,310
the other team still scored too often.

328
00:19:31,420 --> 00:19:34,250
Sora's lack of height is a 
pretty big problem for us, huh?

329
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:39,170
If I coached the other team,
that is definitely where I would focus my attack.

330
00:19:40,130 --> 00:19:41,670
So that means you're on the bench!

331
00:19:42,330 --> 00:19:43,880
No! Anything but that!

332
00:19:44,250 --> 00:19:47,540
Needless to say, we can't afford
to just leave Kurumatani off the court.

333
00:19:47,540 --> 00:19:51,210
Having a three-point shooter like him
is a huge benefit to us.

334
00:19:53,210 --> 00:19:57,040
We also need him out there to help spread out
the other team's defense.

335
00:19:57,290 --> 00:19:58,640
With that said,

336
00:19:58,640 --> 00:20:00,690
I'm proposing that we make this
the basic pattern for our defense.

337
00:20:00,690 --> 00:20:02,030
Take a look.

338
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,210
Interesting. That's a good plan.

339
00:20:05,210 --> 00:20:07,210
Wait a sec, does this mean that I...?

340
00:20:07,710 --> 00:20:10,420
Starting tomorrow, we'll practice
this formation together with our offense

341
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:12,880
until everyone has mastered it completely.

342
00:20:13,670 --> 00:20:16,790
And in order to make this 
defense absolutely perfect...

343
00:20:16,960 --> 00:20:21,170
...Kurumatani will need to return back to doing
footwork practice by himself tomorrow.

344
00:20:26,290 --> 00:20:29,710
The defense is getting shaken off!
Look carefully before you pass!

345
00:20:48,710 --> 00:20:50,630
The water went in my nose!

346
00:20:51,790 --> 00:20:53,040
Here, use this.

347
00:20:55,080 --> 00:20:56,290
Th-thanks...

348
00:20:57,130 --> 00:20:59,170
Sorry. Are you mad?

349
00:20:59,170 --> 00:21:01,500
Huh?! I'm not mad at all.

350
00:21:01,500 --> 00:21:02,420
Why?

351
00:21:02,750 --> 00:21:06,210
I mean... I made you practice separately
from everyone else.

352
00:21:06,210 --> 00:21:08,080
I feel like I'm being a bully...

353
00:21:08,080 --> 00:21:10,380
I don't mind, since that's 
what we need to win.

354
00:21:10,710 --> 00:21:11,790
But...

355
00:21:12,670 --> 00:21:14,920
I want to win... really bad.

356
00:21:16,250 --> 00:21:18,080
It becomes clearer the 
longer that we practice.

357
00:21:18,380 --> 00:21:22,040
Everyone is gradually starting
to trust each other more as they play.

358
00:21:22,790 --> 00:21:27,420
I can tell everyone has started to believe...
that our team really has a shot at this.

359
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:34,710
Back when we played against Maru High,
there was really nothing that went in our favor.

360
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:38,250
But despite all of that,
it was still really frustrating to lose.

361
00:21:38,880 --> 00:21:41,170
Back then, if we had a stronger defense...

362
00:21:41,960 --> 00:21:44,000
Back then, if my shots 
hadn't missed the mark...

363
00:21:45,380 --> 00:21:47,210
I want to experience more 
than just regrets like those.

364
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:50,460
I want to know what it feels like
to share the joy of victory with a team.

365
00:21:52,210 --> 00:21:53,040
Yeah.

366
00:21:53,880 --> 00:21:55,250
You guys can definitely win.

367
00:21:57,500 --> 00:21:58,500
Yeah!

368
00:23:30,960 --> 00:23:35,420
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: The Boys' Spirit

369
00:23:31,460 --> 00:23:34,580
Next time: "The Boys' Spirit."

